# Copy to .env and fill in. Only ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is required for live generation.
# The offline commands (selftest, practice --demo, checkbatch, plan) need none of these.
# Every setting and its default is in the README's Configuration table.

ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-your-key-here

# --- optional overrides (examples; the default is noted where it differs) ---
# BJT_MODEL=claude-opus-5           # generator model (default claude-sonnet-5)
# BJT_JUDGE_MODEL=claude-opus-5     # gate, discriminator and picture reviewer (default claude-sonnet-5)
# BJT_DB_PATH=bjt.db
# BJT_SEEDS_DIR=seeds
# BJT_GATE_TRIALS=3
# BJT_SPEND_LEDGER=/tmp/night-spend.json   # steps of one job share one budget and clock (CI sets it)

# --- difficulty probe with Jev (a prototype; bjt/jev.py) ---
# Compare first: `bjt probe --all --compare jev-latest` writes nothing. Setting
# BJT_DIFFICULTY_MODEL makes `bjt probe` write Jev's rates into the bundles.
# TYPESAFE_API_KEY=...
# BJT_DIFFICULTY_MODEL=jev-latest       # default claude-haiku-4-5

# --- pictures (bjt scenes --generate) ---
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...                 # the image model; ANTHROPIC_API_KEY reviews each draft
# BJT_IMAGE_MODEL=gpt-image-1
# BJT_IMAGE_QUALITY=high                # default medium
# BJT_SCENE_ATTEMPTS=3                  # drafts the review may refuse per picture per run

# --- audio (bjt synth, bjt audition) ---
# The library's voice is OpenAI (DEFAULT in bjt/tts/providers.py); the same
# OPENAI_API_KEY above is all `bjt synth` needs. `bjt audition` writes the cast
# side by side (and with --voices, every voice the model offers) for a person
# to listen to.
# BJT_OPENAI_TTS_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini-tts
# BJT_TTS_PROVIDER=gemini               # laptop-only override, to compare another provider
# GEMINI_API_KEY=...                    # only for that comparison

# --- uploading pictures and audio (bjt scenes --upload, bjt synth --upload) ---
# An R2 API token's S3 pair (Cloudflare dashboard → R2 → Manage API tokens),
# scoped to the media bucket with object read and write. It writes media, so it
# belongs here or in a GitHub secret, never in client/ and never in a commit.
# R2_ACCOUNT_ID=...                     # the Cloudflare account id
# R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID=...
# R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=...
# R2_BUCKET=business-japanese-drill-media
